Robolectric's changeDisplay(qualifiers) leaves the display-change messages to the app's run loop (apklayer patch).

Against external/robolectric 87aa52b08 (REVISION). Applied by runtime/meson.build onto the staged
upstream sources (<native>/aosp/robolectric-src); the result is compiled into native-runtime.jar ahead of Robolectric_all.jar.
---
diff --git a/shadows/framework/src/main/java/org/robolectric/shadows/ShadowDisplayManager.java b/shadows/framework/src/main/java/org/robolectric/shadows/ShadowDisplayManager.java
--- a/shadows/framework/src/main/java/org/robolectric/shadows/ShadowDisplayManager.java
+++ b/shadows/framework/src/main/java/org/robolectric/shadows/ShadowDisplayManager.java
@@ -247,7 +247,8 @@
   public static void changeDisplay(int displayId, String qualifiersStr) {
     DisplayInfo displayInfo = createDisplayInfo(qualifiersStr, displayId);
     getShadowDisplayManagerGlobal().changeDisplay(displayId, displayInfo);
-    shadowMainLooper().idle();
+    // apklayer patch: the app's run loop delivers the display-change messages; an idle here ran until the main queue was empty,
+    // which never happens while an app keeps posting to it (ASTRO at its first window configure)
   }
 
   /**
